-- title:
--   ℚ̄-q-expansion field of Γ inside the level-M function field
-- statement:
--   Let $M\ge 1$, let $\Gamma\le\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb Z)$ contain the principal congruence subgroup $\Gamma(M)$ and the translation matrix $T$, let $\iota:\overline{\mathbb Q}\to\mathbb C$ be a ring homomorphism, and let $K$ be a field that is simultaneously a $\mathbb C$-algebra and an algebra over $A_M:=\mathbb C[\,E_4^3/\Delta,\ \text{fricke}_M(v)\ (v\in(\mathbb Z/M)^2,\ v\neq 0)\,]\subseteq(\mathcal H\to\mathbb C)$, compatibly as a scalar tower, and is a fraction field of $A_M$. Write $F:=\overline{\mathbb Q}\!\cdot\!F(\Gamma)$ for the intermediate field of $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}(\overline{\mathbb Q})$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ generated by the coefficientwise image of the field generated over $\mathbb Q$ by the quotients $\mathrm{intSeriesC}\,p_f/\mathrm{intSeriesC}\,p_g$ of integral $q$-expansions of modular forms of equal weight for $\Gamma$. Then there exist a ring homomorphism $\Phi:F\to K$ and a $\mathbb C$-algebra homomorphism $E:K\to\mathrm{LaurentSeries}(\mathbb C)$ such that: $E$ sends the image of $E_4^3/\Delta$ to $\mathrm{qExpand}_M$ of the $j$-series $q^{-1}\cdot\mathrm{jNum}$; $E(\Phi u)=\mathrm{qExpand}_M(\iota_* u)$ for all $u\in F$; $\Phi$ restricted to constants is $\iota$ followed by $\mathbb C\to K$; any $y\in F$ whose underlying series is the $j$-series over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ has $\Phi y$ the image of $E_4^3/\Delta$; for every $\gamma\in\Gamma$ such that $G\mapsto G(\gamma^{-1}\cdot)$ preserves $A_M$, every $\mathbb C$-algebra automorphism $\varphi$ of $K$ inducing that substitution on $A_M$ fixes $\Phi u$ for all $u\in F$; and, for every $\Gamma'\ge\Gamma$ and every $\gamma\in\Gamma'$ with the same stability hypothesis, such a $\varphi$ fixes $\Phi u$ for every $u\in F$ whose underlying Laurent series lies in $\overline{\mathbb Q}\!\cdot\!F(\Gamma')$.
--
--   This is the rationality statement placing the $q$-expansion field of level $\Gamma$, base changed to $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ via $\iota$, inside a fraction field of the level-$M$ algebra of $j$ and Fricke functions, compatibly with $q$-expansions and with the substitution action of $\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb Z)$, in the style of Shimura and of Diamond–Shurman. The final clause, recording invariance under substitutions by elements of any overgroup $\Gamma'$ for elements expanding inside the level-$\Gamma'$ field, is what the subsequent computation of the ramification index of the inclusion of $\Gamma_0$-level in $\Gamma_H$-level function fields uses.
